   ],
   "start_page": 1,
   "summary": "These registry sheets compile sub-numbers 41 through 179 of State Department decimal file 894.24, covering the period from February 1932 to March 1938. They document widespread intelligence tracking Japanese efforts to acquire strategic raw materials and military supplies—such as scrap iron and steel, crude oil, aviation fuel, copper, plumbago, nitrates, aircraft, and armaments—from the Americas, Europe, and Asia. The entries also record escalating domestic inquiries and protests from American citizens, labor groups, and corporate representatives regarding arms shipments, together with repeated State Department replies affirming the lack of statutory authority to restrict private exports under existing laws.",
   "title": "List of Papers: State Department Decimal File 894.24 (Army Equipment - Japan)",
   "to": ""
  },
